    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0613" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg565"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Browne</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 17, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your letter, written at San Francisco on
                    the 24th of July last, has been received. It is accompanied by a correspondence
                    which has taken place between yourself and Mr. George Wilkes, director of the
                    Lower California Company, on the subject of emigration from China to Lower
                    California.</p>
                <p>I see nothing to disapprove of in your letter to Mr. Wilkes. The emigration
                    movement which is the subject of this correspondence will doubtless prove
                    beneficial, if justly, wisely, and generously conducted. I am, sir, your
                    obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Ross Browne,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
